OFFICIAL-SENSITIVE

Cumbria Resilience Forum - Storm Fenella - SITREP 7
Time of report: 15/01/2026 1300

1. SITUATION
Incident status: ACTIVE - response
Rainfall totals of 120-180 mm recorded at upland gauges.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- Pooley Bridge crossing: closed to all traffic
- M6 Junction 40: OPEN
- Northside Bridge, Workington: closed to all traffic
- A66 west of Penrith: reopened
- Glenridding village hall: operating as a rest centre (run by WFC)
- A591 at Thirlmere: closed - flooding
- West Coast Main Line (Carlisle to Lancaster): reopened (run by NR)
- Queen Elizabeth School: open to pupils
- Cockermouth School: operating as a rest centre (run by Cumberland Cuoncil)
- Riverside Community Centre: operating as a rest centre
- Keswick School: rest centre OPEN (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- Fellside: evacuated (run by Fellside Care)

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
NCIC Trust, National Highways North West, EA

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 1800. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

